    11	#         all four sides through the middle row and middle column.
    12	#       - Outside the cross, the four corner quadrants are filled by one of two small
    13	#         libraries. In "top_lift" mode, each quadrant contains a vertical domino near
    14	#         the top/bottom edge plus an oriented L-triomino near the cross. In
    15	#         "bottom_lift" mode, the domino family is replaced by eight border singletons
    16	#         and the L-triominoes move upward/downward accordingly.
    17	#       - The strengthened D5 rule is visible in the finished board: when one color is
    18	#         reused across multiple pieces, any two distinct same-color components are kept
    19	#         at Chebyshev distance >= 2. Diagonal touching never occurs.
    20	#     input:
    21	#       - The 11-cell cross frame stays grouped as one untranslated patch inside the
    22	#         input, preserving the "recognizable anchor" idea from the source task.
    23	#       - All non-frame pieces are scattered separately with 8-neighborhood padding, so
    24	#         the solver must recover the compact rectangle from disconnected fragments.
    25	#     trace_example:
    26	#       - Original logic: after finding a frame, a top-left fragment only needed to
    27	#         respect left-right mirroring; an equally shaped counterpart could still float
    28	#         between an upper slot and a lower slot if both preserved LR symmetry.
    29	#       - Fused logic here: the chosen library fixes four quadrant roles at once. A
    30	#         fragment placed in the upper half immediately determines the lower-half mirror,
    31	#         and the final board is rejected unless every repeated color also stays clear of
    32	#         diagonal same-color contact. The dual-axis rule and the 8-neighbor rule act on
    33	#         the same quadrant inventory, rather than as unrelated post-filters.
    34	#   complexity_calibration:
    35	#     - The rectangle remains compact and puzzle-like, but the grouped frame is now a
    36	#       cross rather than the old zigzag border because diagonal same-color chaining is
    37	#       illegal under D5/0.
    38	#     - Only two quadrant libraries are used. That is enough variation for training
    39	#       examples to show that multiple fused layouts exist, while keeping the object
    40	#       vocabulary small and learnable.
    41	#     - Piece counts stay in the original visual band: 13 pieces in top_lift mode and
    42	#       17 pieces in bottom_lift mode. Colors stay at exactly four.
    43	#   implicit_assumption_review:
    44	#     - Old _assemble() assumed LR reflection was the only global orbit constraint.
    45	#       That no longer holds; the fused solver must reason in full 4-way orbits.
    46	#     - Old sparse-frame generation relied on diagonal same-color contacts to keep a
    47	#       single color visually connected under 8-connectivity. That violates D5/0, so the
    48	#       fused generator replaces it with a single 4-connected cross component.
    49	#     - The source solver inferred arbitrary output shapes from area. Here the frame
    50	#       library is deliberately fixed to area 35, so the solver now assumes the unique
    51	#       closest-to-square factorization is 7x5 and the generator guarantees that.
    52	#     - Because the quadrant library is fixed, the solver assumes exactly one cross
    53	#       component of area 11, exactly one 4-corner singleton color, and then one of two
    54	#       remaining inventories: {4 vertical dominoes + 4 oriented L-triominoes} or
    55	#       {8 border singletons + 4 oriented L-triominoes}. The generator enforces this.
    56	#   placement_legality:
    57	#     - The generator builds the final 7x5 board first, validates dual symmetry and the
    58	#       8-neighbor same-color gap, extracts each 4-connected component as an immutable
    59	#       piece, then scatters them onto a 13-15 square canvas with Chebyshev padding 1.
    60	#     - The cross frame is pasted as one grouped patch inside a blocked bbox, so other
    61	#       pieces never overlap it or leak into the final rectangle interior.
    62	#   observability:
    63	#     - Humans can see the fused change from a few examples because the output is not
    64	#       merely LR-symmetric: the top half and bottom half are exact mirrors, and the
    65	#       repeated colors form a checkerboard-like spacing with no diagonal same-color
    66	#       kisses.
    67	#     - The two modes visibly differ in where the non-corner border fragments sit: one
    68	#       mode has four 2-cell vertical bars, the other has eight isolated border pixels.
    69	#       That repeated contrast provides enough support for inferring the library.
    70	#   cleanliness:
    71	#     - The output has three clearly separated layers: four corner anchors, one central
    72	#       cross frame, and one quadrant-piece library. No region carries more than one
    73	#       structural role.
    74	#   inferability:
    75	#     - Color remapping is sample-local and unconstrained by numeric ids. The only
    76	#       stable clues are piece shape and position relative to the frame, which are both
    77	#       visually available to a human solver.
